  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(34, 12, 10)\n\n(56, 17, 22)\n\n**Logic:** First no. = [(Second no. × 2) + Third no.]\n\n**(34, 12, 10) →**\n\n⇒ [(12 × 2) + 10]\n\n⇒ (24 + 10) = 34\n\n**(56, 17, 22) →**\n\n⇒ [(17 × 2) + 22]\n\n⇒ (34 + 22) = 56\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1.** (56, 19, 8)\n\n⇒ [(19 × 2) + 8]\n\n⇒ (38 + 8) = 46\n\n**2. (46, 19, 8)**\n\n⇒ [(19 × 2) + 8]\n\n⇒ (38 + 8) = **46**\n\n**3. **(46, 19, 18)\n\n⇒ [(19 × 2) + 18]\n\n⇒ (38 + 18) = 56\n\n**4.** (46, 49, 8)\n\n⇒ [(49 × 2) + 8]\n\n⇒ (98 + 8) = 106\n\nHere, **(46, 19, 8)** shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (2)\".",
